# AWS Systems Manager User Guide

> AWS Systems Manager (formerly Amazon EC2 Systems Manager) is a unified interface that lets you centralize operational data and automate tasks across your AWS resources. Systems Manager shortens the time to detect and resolve operational problems in your infrastructure. Systems Manager gives you a complete view of your infrastructure performance and configuration, simplifies resource and application management, and lets you operate and manage your infrastructure at scale.

- [AWS Systems Manager Change Manager availability change](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/change-manager-availability-change.md)
- [Related information](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/related-information.md)
- [Document history](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/systems-manager-release-history.md)
- [Document conventions](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/docconventions.md)

