## [Setting up managed nodes for AWS Systems Manager](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/systems-manager-setting-up-nodes.md)

### [Managing EC2 instances with Systems Manager](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/systems-manager-setting-up-ec2.md)

Learn how to set up Systems Manager to configure and manage the EC2 instances in your account.

- [Configure instance permissions required for Systems Manager](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/setup-instance-permissions.md): Learn how to configure Amazon EC2 instance permissions for Systems Manager using the Default Host Management Configuration, or an IAM instance profile.
- [Improve the security of EC2 instances by using VPC endpoints for Systems Manager](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/setup-create-vpc.md): Discover how to improve the security posture of your managed instances by configuring Systems Manager to use an interface VPC endpoint in Amazon VPC.

### [Managing nodes in hybrid and multicloud environments with Systems Manager](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/systems-manager-hybrid-multicloud.md)

Learn how to set up Systems Manager to configure and manage non-EC2 machines for use in a hybrid and multicloud environment.

- [Create the IAM service role required for Systems Manager in hybrid and multicloud environments](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/hybrid-multicloud-service-role.md): Learn how to grant AssumeRole trust to the Systems Manager service so that it can communicate with non-EC2 machines in hybrid and multicloud environments.
- [Create a hybrid activation to register nodes with Systems Manager](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/hybrid-activation-managed-nodes.md): Learn how to create a managed-node activation to provide secure access to the Systems Manager service from your managed nodes.
- [Install SSM Agent on hybrid Linux nodes](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/hybrid-multicloud-ssm-agent-install-linux.md): Learn how to install SSM Agent on non-EC2 Linux machines in a hybrid and multicloud environment.
- [Install SSM Agent on hybrid Windows Server nodes](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/hybrid-multicloud-ssm-agent-install-windows.md): Learn how to install SSM Agent on non-EC2 Windows Server machines in a hybrid and multicloud environment.
- [Set up Systems Manager for Microsoft Azure virtual machines](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/hybrid-multicloud-ssm-agent-install-azure.md): Learn how to register Microsoft Azure virtual machines as managed nodes in Systems Manager using native Azure cloud provider integration.

### [Set up a Cloud Connector for Microsoft Azure in Systems Manager](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/systems-manager-cloud-connector.md)

Learn how to create a Systems Manager Cloud Connector to manage Azure virtual machines as managed nodes.

- [Create a Cloud Connector (AWS Management Console)](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/cloud-connector-create-console.md): We recommend that you use the AWS Management Console to create a Cloud Connector.

### [Prerequisites](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/cloud-connector-prerequisites.md)

Before you create a Cloud Connector, complete the following prerequisites on both the AWS side and the Azure side.

- [AWS prerequisites](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/cloud-connector-prereqs-aws.md): Complete the following steps in your AWS account.
- [Azure prerequisites](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/cloud-connector-prereqs-azure.md): Complete the following steps in your Azure environment.
- [Step 1: Create an AWS Config connector](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/cloud-connector-create-config-connector.md): The AWS Config connector sets up the credential exchange between AWS and Azure and enables AWS Config to record Azure resource state.
- [Step 2: Create a Systems Manager Cloud Connector](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/cloud-connector-create-ssm-connector.md): After the AWS Config connector is set up, create the Systems Manager Cloud Connector.
- [Manage Cloud Connectors](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/cloud-connector-manage.md): Use the following AWS CLI commands to manage your Cloud Connectors.

### [Enable VM onboarding](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/cloud-connector-enable-vm-onboarding.md)

Learn how Systems Manager uses State Manager associations and Automation to install SSM Agent on Azure VMs and register them as managed instances.

- [Enable VM onboarding (AWS Management Console)](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/cloud-connector-onboarding-console.md): To enable VM onboarding in the AWS Management Console:
- [Enable VM onboarding (AWS CLI)](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/cloud-connector-onboarding-cli.md): To enable VM onboarding using the AWS CLI, create a State Manager association that targets the Cloud Connector.

### [IAM roles created by the Systems Manager console](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/cloud-connector-console-iam-roles.md)

Reference for the IAM roles that Systems Manager creates on your behalf when you set up a Cloud Connector for Microsoft Azure in the AWS Management Console, including their trust policies and permissions policies.

- [Azure federation role](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/cloud-connector-azure-federation-role.md): The Azure federation role lets Systems Manager obtain a web identity token from AWS Security Token Service (AWS STS) and exchange it for Azure credentials through OIDC federation.
- [Automation assume role](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/cloud-connector-automation-assume-role.md): The automation assume role is the role Automation assumes when it runs the runbook that onboards an Azure virtual machine as a managed node.
- [Automation dispatch role](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/cloud-connector-automation-dispatch-role.md): The automation dispatch role is the role State Manager uses when it starts an Automation execution against a Cloud Connector.
- [Managed instance role](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/cloud-connector-managed-instance-role.md): The managed instance role is the IAM role that SSM Agent assumes on each Azure virtual machine after it's installed and registered.
- [Tags applied to managed instances](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/cloud-connector-managed-instance-tags.md): When Systems Manager onboards an Azure virtual machine through a Cloud Connector, it automatically applies the following tag to the resulting managed instance.
- [How Systems Manager handles cloud resources](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/cloud-connector-identifiers.md): By enabling Multicloud Integrations for AWS Systems Manager, virtual machine identifiers from other cloud providers are stored in Systems Manager and other AWS services as needed.
- [Managing edge devices with Systems Manager](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/systems-manager-setting-up-edge-devices.md): Learn how to set up AWS Systems Manager to configure and manage edge devices.
- [Creating an AWS Organizations delegated administrator for Systems Manager](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/setting_up_delegated_admin.md): Learn how to set up a delegated administrator for Systems Manager.


